
Step 0: Setup (ekbar)
/system clock set time-zone-name=Asia/Dhaka
/system scheduler remove [find name~"check-"]
/system scheduler remove [find name~"daily-"]
/ip hotspot user set [find profile=Hotspot-2h] limit-uptime=0s
/ip hotspot user set [find profile=Hotspot-5min] limit-uptime=0s
 


Script 1: On Login (duita profile e same script)
///////////////////---------------------/////////////////////
[Mikrotik_CLI] /ip/hotspot/profile>Scripts  On Login: 

:if ([/ip hotspot user get [find name=$user] comment] = "") do={
  /ip hotspot user set [find name=$user] comment="days:31"
}

///////////////////---------------------/////////////////////
Note: The reason for setting it to 31 days is that the first day is only
a partial day.Therefore, at midnight on the first night, the validity will
become days:30, ensuring that the user gets the full 30 days of validity.

  




Script 2: Scheduler check-daily-limit 
///////////////////---------------------/////////////////////

[Mikrotik_CLI] System/Scheduler/Add

Name: check-daily-limit
Start Time: 00:00:00
Interval: 00:01:00
On Event:


:foreach i in=[/ip hotspot user find where disabled=no] do={
  :local p [/ip hotspot user get $i profile]
  :local lim 0s
  :if ($p="Hotspot-2h") do={:set lim 02:00:00}
  :if ($p="Hotspot-5min") do={:set lim 00:05:00}
  :if ($lim > 0s) do={
    :local n [/ip hotspot user get $i name]
    :local t [/ip hotspot user get $i uptime]
    :foreach a in=[/ip hotspot active find where user=$n] do={
      :set t ($t + [/ip hotspot active get $a uptime])
    }
    :if ($t >= $lim) do={
      /ip hotspot user set $i disabled=yes
      /ip hotspot active remove [find user=$n]
      /ip hotspot cookie remove [find user=$n]
    }
  }
}

///////////////////---------------------/////////////////////

Note: When the daily usage limit (2 hours or 5 minutes) is reached,
the system disables the user, terminates their active session, and
deletes their cookie.



Script 3: Scheduler daily-reset
///////////////////---------------------/////////////////////

[Mikrotik_CLI] System/Scheduler/Add

Name: daily-reset
Start Time: 00:00:00
Interval: 1d 00:00:00
On Event:


/ip hotspot user reset-counters [/ip hotspot user find where profile="Daily_2h_Validity_3din"]
:foreach i in=[/ip hotspot user find where profile="Daily_2h_Validity_3din" and comment~"^days:"] do={
  :local c [/ip hotspot user get $i comment]
  :local d [:tonum [:pick $c 5 [:len $c]]]
  :local n [/ip hotspot user get $i name]
  :if ($d <= 1) do={
    /ip hotspot user set $i disabled=yes comment="expired"
    /ip hotspot active remove [/ip hotspot active find where user=$n]
    /ip hotspot cookie remove [/ip hotspot cookie find where user=$n]
  } else={
    /ip hotspot user set $i disabled=no comment=("days:" . ($d - 1))
  }
}




///////////////////---------------------/////////////////////
Note: Every day at midnight (12:00 AM), the system:
Resets the daily uptime counter to 0 for all Hotspot-2h and Hotspot-5min users.
For users with a "days:N" comment, it reduces the remaining validity by 1 day
and re-enables the user (so users disabled by the daily limit can log in again).
When the remaining validity reaches days:1, the next midnight marks the user
as "expired", disables the account, and removes the active session and cookie.




